# COVERAGE FIXTURE. Deliberate test data, not an ontology about anything.
#
# RULE: eq-sym
# W3C OWL 2 Web Ontology Language Profiles (Second Edition), section 4.3,
# Table 4: The Semantics of Equality.
# https://www.w3.org/TR/owl2-profiles/#Reasoning_in_OWL_2_RL_and_RDF_Graphs_using_Rules
#
#   T(?x, owl:sameAs, ?y)
#     ->  T(?y, owl:sameAs, ?x)
#
# WHY IT EXISTS. No document in this repository asserts owl:sameAs, so
# tools/horn_differential.py compared the Rust and Python engines on eq-sym zero
# times and its clean sweep said nothing about it.
#
# EXPECTED: exactly one derivation, credited to eq-sym:
#   :b owl:sameAs :a
#
# eq-sym then fires on its own conclusion and re-derives ":a owl:sameAs :b",
# which is asserted, so the closure is reached in one round.
#
# The table holds eq-sym alone out of the eq-* family: none of eq-ref, eq-trans
# or the eq-rep-* replacement rules is a built-in here, so nothing in this file
# propagates the identity into any other triple.

@prefix : <http://ex.org/cover/eq-sym#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .

:a owl:sameAs :b .
